From: nuc-bios-build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: UNDI/SNP for the onboard NIC, and prune the rest

Two related changes to what BDS offers as a network boot device.

1. Publish SNP for the onboard I218-V.

Nothing in this payload did. UefiPayloadPkg carries prebuilt Realtek and ASIX
UNDI blobs and no Intel one, and SnpDxe only layers SNP over an existing
UNDI/NII instance, so the BMC's CDC-ECM gadget was the only network interface
the firmware exposed. Measured on hardware 2026-08-04:

    NucRedfishSync: 2 SNP handle(s) in the system
    NucRedfishSync:   SNP[0] DA:A7:62:23:3E:F5
    NucRedfishSync:   SNP[1] DA:A7:62:23:3E:F5

Both the gadget; the LOM (B8:AE:ED:7E:3F:6E) absent. A chainloaded iPXE snp.efi
-- what Tinkerbell boots -- has no native drivers and binds SNP handles only, so
it had nothing to netboot from and retried DHCP over the management link until
it hit its retry limit.

The driver is iPXE built as a UEFI driver (bin-x86_64-efi/intel.efidrv, via
interface/efi/efi_snp.c), embedded next to the Realtek and ASIX blobs. It is
gated on its own NETWORK_IPXE_UNDI define rather than NETWORK_IPXE, because the
iPXE boot *application* is a separate thing and is not wanted here.

2. Prune the boot options nobody should see.

EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption() creates a PXEv4 option for every network
interface it can boot from, which on this board yields:

    PXEv4 (MAC:B8AEED7E3F6E)        PciRoot()/Pci(0x19,0)/MAC()
    PXEv4 (MAC:B8AEED7E3F6E) 2      PciRoot()/Pci(0x19,0)/MAC()/IPv4()
    PXEv4 (MAC:DAA762233EF5)        the BMC host interface, over USB

The onboard NIC appears twice because iPXE's UNDI driver installs SNP *and*
NII31 on one handle. The two are not interchangeable: only the NII31 entry --
the one carrying an IPv4 node, because the UEFI PXE stack layered Ip4 on it --
actually boots. Selecting the bare SNP one fails at BDS with

    Booting from 'PXEv4 (MAC:B8AEED7E3F6E)' failed: Not Found

and, with nothing to fall back to, leaves the machine at a "Press any key to
continue" prompt. So for each MAC keep the option carrying an IPv4 node and drop
the rest, rather than keeping whichever came first.

The third entry is the management link, which has no DHCP server and is not a
boot path. It is recognised by a USB node in its device path -- no USB-attached
NIC on this board is a boot device -- which keeps the check free of any
dependency on the Redfish package.

Finally the " 2" BDS appended to disambiguate the duplicate is stripped, since
after pruning there is nothing left to disambiguate against.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform specific]
Signed-off-by: nuc-bios-build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c	2026-08-04 10:12:32.423293206 -0500
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c	2026-08-04 10:46:05.166878339 -0500
@@ -441,6 +441,176 @@
   PlatformConsoleInit ();
 }
 
+
+/**
+  Tidy the auto-created network boot options.
+
+  EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption() creates a PXEv4 option for every network
+  interface it can boot from, which on this board yields three entries where
+  only one is wanted:
+
+    PXEv4 (MAC:B8AEED7E3F6E)        PciRoot()/Pci(0x19,0)/MAC()
+    PXEv4 (MAC:B8AEED7E3F6E) 2      PciRoot()/Pci(0x19,0)/MAC()/IPv4()
+    PXEv4 (MAC:DAA762233EF5)        the BMC host interface, over USB
+
+  The onboard NIC appears twice because iPXE's UNDI driver installs SNP *and*
+  NII31 on one handle. The two are not interchangeable: only the NII31 one --
+  the one carrying an IPv4 node, because the UEFI PXE stack layered Ip4 on it --
+  actually boots. Selecting the other fails at BDS with
+
+      Booting from 'PXEv4 (MAC:B8AEED7E3F6E)' failed: Not Found
+
+  and, having no fallback, leaves the machine sitting at a "Press any key to
+  continue" prompt. So for each MAC keep the option with an IPv4 node and drop
+  the rest, rather than keeping whichever came first.
+
+  The host interface goes entirely. It exists for Redfish (DSP0270), has no DHCP
+  server on it, and is not a boot path. Recognised by a USB node in its device
+  path -- no USB-attached NIC on this board is a boot device -- which keeps this
+  free of any dependency on the Redfish package.
+
+  Finally, drop the " 2" that BDS appended to disambiguate the duplicate, since
+  after pruning there is nothing left to disambiguate against.
+
+  Only auto-created options are considered; anything an OS installer or an
+  operator wrote is left alone.
+**/
+STATIC
+VOID
+PruneAutoCreatedNetworkBootOptions (
+  VOID
+  )
+{
+  EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION  *Options;
+  EFI_DEVICE_PATH_PROTOCOL      *Node;
+  MAC_ADDR_DEVICE_PATH          *Mac;
+  UINTN                         OptionCount;
+  UINTN                         Index;
+  UINTN                         Other;
+  UINTN                         Length;
+  BOOLEAN                       Drop;
+  EFI_MAC_ADDRESS               *MacOf[16];
+  BOOLEAN                       HasIp4[16];
+  BOOLEAN                       OverUsb[16];
+  CHAR16                        *Desc;
+
+  Options = EfiBootManagerGetLoadOptions (&OptionCount, LoadOptionTypeBoot);
+  if ((Options == NULL) || (OptionCount == 0)) {
+    return;
+  }
+
+  if (OptionCount > ARRAY_SIZE (MacOf)) {
+    OptionCount = ARRAY_SIZE (MacOf);
+  }
+
+  //
+  // Classify every option first: deleting as we go would mean deciding about
+  // one entry before having seen the one that should outrank it.
+  //
+  for (Index = 0; Index < OptionCount; Index++) {
+    MacOf[Index]   = NULL;
+    HasIp4[Index]  = FALSE;
+    OverUsb[Index] = FALSE;
+
+    if (Options[Index].FilePath == NULL) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    for (Node = Options[Index].FilePath; !IsDevicePathEnd (Node); Node = NextDevicePathNode (Node)) {
+      if (DevicePathType (Node) != MESSAGING_DEVICE_PATH) {
+        continue;
+      }
+
+      switch (DevicePathSubType (Node)) {
+        case MSG_USB_DP:
+          OverUsb[Index] = TRUE;
+          break;
+        case MSG_IPv4_DP:
+          HasIp4[Index] = TRUE;
+          break;
+        case MSG_MAC_ADDR_DP:
+          Mac          = (MAC_ADDR_DEVICE_PATH *)Node;
+          MacOf[Index] = &Mac->MacAddress;
+          break;
+        default:
+          break;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
+  for (Index = 0; Index < OptionCount; Index++) {
+    //
+    // Not a network option at all.
+    //
+    if (MacOf[Index] == NULL) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    Drop = OverUsb[Index];
+
+    //
+    // Outranked by another option for the same NIC?
+    //
+    for (Other = 0; (Other < OptionCount) && !Drop; Other++) {
+      if ((Other == Index) || (MacOf[Other] == NULL) || OverUsb[Other]) {
+        continue;
+      }
+
+      if (CompareMem (MacOf[Other], MacOf[Index], sizeof (EFI_MAC_ADDRESS)) != 0) {
+        continue;
+      }
+
+      if (HasIp4[Other] && !HasIp4[Index]) {
+        //
+        // The NII31 entry boots; the bare SNP one does not.
+        //
+        Drop = TRUE;
+      } else if ((HasIp4[Other] == HasIp4[Index]) && (Other < Index)) {
+        Drop = TRUE;
+      }
+    }
+
+    if (Drop) {
+      DEBUG ((
+        DEBUG_INFO,
+        "%a: dropping Boot%04x (%a)\n",
+        __func__,
+        Options[Index].OptionNumber,
+        OverUsb[Index] ? "USB host interface" : "outranked duplicate"
+        ));
+      EfiBootManagerDeleteLoadOptionVariable (Options[Index].OptionNumber, LoadOptionTypeBoot);
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    //
+    // Survivor: strip a trailing " <n>" disambiguator, if BDS added one.
+    //
+    Desc = Options[Index].Description;
+    if (Desc == NULL) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
+    Length = StrLen (Desc);
+    while ((Length > 0) && (Desc[Length - 1] >= L'0') && (Desc[Length - 1] <= L'9')) {
+      Length--;
+    }
+
+    if ((Length > 1) && (Length < StrLen (Desc)) && (Desc[Length - 1] == L' ')) {
+      Desc[Length - 1] = L'\0';
+      EfiBootManagerLoadOptionToVariable (&Options[Index]);
+      DEBUG ((
+        DEBUG_INFO,
+        "%a: renamed Boot%04x to \"%s\"\n",
+        __func__,
+        Options[Index].OptionNumber,
+        Desc
+        ));
+    }
+  }
+
+  EfiBootManagerFreeLoadOptions (Options, OptionCount);
+}
+
 /**
   Do the platform specific action after the console is connected.
 
@@ -475,6 +645,8 @@
   EfiBootManagerConnectAll ();
   EfiBootManagerRefreshAllBootOption ();
 
+  PruneAutoCreatedNetworkBootOptions ();
+
   //
   // Active BOOT_ON_FLASH_UPDATE mode means that at least one capsule has been
   // discovered by a bootloader and passed for further processing into EDK which
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc	2026-08-04 10:10:31.774304187 -0500
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dsc	2026-08-04 10:10:31.774355242 -0500
@@ -201,6 +201,7 @@
   DEFINE NETWORK_ASIX_USB2              = FALSE
   DEFINE NETWORK_SNP_ENABLE             = FALSE
   DEFINE NETWORK_IPXE                   = FALSE
+  DEFINE NETWORK_IPXE_UNDI              = FALSE
 
 !if $(NETWORK_PXE_BOOT) == TRUE
   DEFINE NETWORK_ENABLE                 = TRUE
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf	2026-08-04 10:10:31.774451063 -0500
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf	2026-08-04 10:10:31.774484943 -0500
@@ -504,6 +504,15 @@
 !if $(ARCH) == IA32
   # FIXME
 !else
+# NucRedfish: UNDI/SNP for the onboard LOM. Nothing else in this payload
+# publishes EFI_SIMPLE_NETWORK_PROTOCOL for it, so a boot client that binds
+# SNP handles only -- iPXE's snp.efi, which Tinkerbell chainloads -- saw just
+# the BMC's host interface and had nothing to netboot from.
+!if $(NETWORK_IPXE_UNDI) == TRUE
+  FILE DRIVER = F773F4F9-5C3E-475F-AE02-151D514D7379 {
+    SECTION PE32 = UefiPayloadPkg/NetworkDrivers/ipxe-intel.efidrv
+  }
+!endif
 !if $(NETWORK_RTEK_PCI)
   FILE DRIVER = D30D5496-6DF9-462D-9B97-0B93F659D1A0 {
     SECTION PE32 = UefiPayloadPkg/NetworkDrivers/RtkUndiDxe.efi
